From: Stanislaw Pal <kuncy7@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 13:40:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] net: stmmac: dwmac1000: keep PAUSE frames out of the receive
 path in promiscuous mode

In promiscuous mode dwmac1000 sets PCF to 0b10: every MAC control frame
is passed to the application. A PAUSE frame is acted on by the flow
control logic of the MAC regardless, so passing it on only hands the
receive path frames the stack throws away.

On an IPQ5018 the GMAC is the conduit of a switch and therefore in
promiscuous mode, and its receive ring belongs to the NSS firmware, which
punts every such frame to the host as an exception. A TP-Link Archer
AX55 talks to its RTL8367S over a 2.5G link; with a client on a 1G port
downloading at ~800 Mb/s the switch paused the GMAC tens of thousands of
times per run, and each PAUSE ended up on the host CPU.

Use PCF 0b01 instead: control frames other than PAUSE still pass, PAUSE
stays with the flow control logic.

Signed-off-by: Stanislaw Pal <kuncy7@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac1000.h
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac1000.h
@@ -125,6 +125,7 @@
 #define GMAC_FRAME_FILTER_PM	0x00000010	/* Pass all multicast */
 #define GMAC_FRAME_FILTER_DBF	0x00000020	/* Disable Broadcast frames */
 #define GMAC_FRAME_FILTER_PCF	0x00000080	/* Pass Control frames */
+#define GMAC_FRAME_FILTER_PCF_NOPAUSE	0x00000040	/* Pass Control frames but PAUSE */
 #define GMAC_FRAME_FILTER_SAIF	0x00000100	/* Inverse Filtering */
 #define GMAC_FRAME_FILTER_SAF	0x00000200	/* Source Address Filter */
 #define GMAC_FRAME_FILTER_HPF	0x00000400	/* Hash or perfect Filter */
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac1000_core.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac1000_core.c
@@ -154,7 +154,12 @@
 	memset(mc_filter, 0, sizeof(mc_filter));
 
 	if (dev->flags & IFF_PROMISC) {
-		value = GMAC_FRAME_FILTER_PR | GMAC_FRAME_FILTER_PCF;
+		/* A PAUSE frame is acted on by the flow control logic of the
+		 * MAC; passing it on as well only feeds the receive path with
+		 * frames the stack drops. Behind an NSS firmware every one of
+		 * them is an exception punted to the host.
+		 */
+		value = GMAC_FRAME_FILTER_PR | GMAC_FRAME_FILTER_PCF_NOPAUSE;
 	} else if (dev->flags & IFF_ALLMULTI) {
 		value = GMAC_FRAME_FILTER_PM;	/* pass all multi */
 	} else if (!netdev_mc_empty(dev) && (mcbitslog2 == 0)) {
